<div style="background-color: #e0f2f7; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin-bottom: 10px;">Lesson Planner – Theme # 3 – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; font-size: 1.1em;"><i>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</i></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Scenario:</b> International Communication</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Theme:</b> Communicating Panama's Importance</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Present a summary of various content including products, entertainment, or recreational activities. Interactive: Debate on topics relevant to current social trends.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can summarize content that highlights Panama's cultural identity, innovations, or contributions as part of introducing the country to the world (e.g., "It is said that Panama has been praised for its efforts in preserving biodiversity.") Can participate in debates on issues related to Panama's national and global significance, presenting clear and well-supported arguments (e.g., "The Panama Canal's expansion has greatly boosted global trade efficiency, which I argue strengthens Panama's position in the international economy.") Can answer questions during a debate, defending or expanding on their argument about the importance of English proficiency to effectively communicate Panama's significance as a global trade location (e.g., "Panama's position as a key trade hub requires clear communication in English to engage international partners and promote economic growth.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0f2f7; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0f2f7; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0f2f7; color: #1a5276; width: 34%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b><br>(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> Students participate in a "Think-Pair-Share" activity. The teacher asks, "What makes Panama a key player on the global stage?" (Stress on WHAT and KEY PLAYER modeled). Students briefly reflect, share with a partner, and then a few volunteers share with the class. This activates prior knowledge from previous lessons on Panama's importance.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models a brief summary using target language: "Panama is recognized for its strategic location, which connects continents. Our biodiversity is often praised, and our professionals must be proficient in English to engage internationally." The teacher emphasizes the pronunciation of /t/ in "strategic" and /g/ in "global" and the stress on "MUST".</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is Panama known only locally or globally?" (Expected answer: "Globally.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Why must professionals be proficient in English?" (Expected answer: "To interact with international partners/clients.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</b><br>(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "International Communication")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Short audio recording (1-2 minutes) of an interview with a Panamanian diplomat or economist discussing Panama's global impact. The audio features sentences like: "The Panama Canal's expansion, which has greatly boosted global trade efficiency, is considered a significant achievement. It is a transit hub where multinational companies are based, requiring robust financial services. Our natural biodiversity is protected, attracting many ecotourists."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> The student can understand general information and specific details of short recorded public announcements and conversations on topics of personal and public relevance.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students listen to the audio twice and answer gist and detail questions orally.</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the main topic of the interview?" (Gist)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"True or False: The Panama Canal's expansion reduced global trade efficiency." (Detail)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What other sectors are mentioned as important for Panama's economy?" (Detail)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b><br>(Accuracy focus on Speaking)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice using the passive voice, modals of necessity, and relative clauses with target vocabulary (e.g., `trade`, `relevance`, `biodiversity`, `proficient`, `hub`, `impact`, `recognize`, `require`, `strategic`, `significant`).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice:</b> Students work in pairs to complete sentence stems orally, focusing on passive voice and modals. Example stems: "Panama ____ (recognize) for its...", "Professionals ____ (must/should) ____ (be proficient) in English...", "The Canal is a trade hub ____ (connect) continents..." They take turns completing the sentences and checking each other's grammar and vocabulary use.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Substitution Drill:</b> Teacher provides a model sentence, e.g., "Panama is considered a global hub, which attracts international companies." Students take turns substituting underlined words with other target vocabulary or information, ensuring the relative clause structure is maintained. Example prompts: `financial services`, `ecotourists`, `scientific area`, `protected biodiversity`. E.g., Student 1: "Panama is considered a global hub, which attracts international companies." Student 2: "Panama is considered a financial services area, which attracts multinational companies." Student 3: "Panama is recognized for its protected biodiversity, which attracts many ecotourists."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction/Peer Check:</b> Students receive prompt cards with keywords (e.g., `Panama Canal`, `biodiversity`, `English proficiency`). In pairs, they create 2-3 sentences about each prompt, using at least one passive voice construction, one modal of necessity, and one relative clause. They orally present their sentences to their partner, who provides feedback on clarity and accuracy.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b><br>(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "International Communication")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Class Debate: "The Importance of English Proficiency for Panama's Global Relevance."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students are divided into two teams: "Affirmative" (English proficiency is absolutely critical for all aspects of Panama's global relevance) and "Negative" (While important, other factors or languages might be equally or more crucial in certain sectors).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each team prepares arguments for 5 minutes, incorporating target grammar (passive voice, modals, relative clauses), and vocabulary (e.g., `global`, `key`, `critical`, `trade`, `commerce`, `financial services`, `ecotourist`, `interact`, `ensure`).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The debate follows a structured format: opening statements (2 min per team), rebuttal/discussion (5 min), and closing statements (1 min per team).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students are encouraged to use phrases showing respect for different opinions (e.g., "From my perspective...", "While I understand your point, I must emphasize...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher acts as a moderator, ensuring all viewpoints are acknowledged and effectively communicated. Pronunciation of /t/, /g/, and stress on modal verbs (e.g., "English MUST be prioritized") is monitored.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">12-15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b><br>(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist focusing on speaking output and a peer assessment rubric for the debate.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students' active participation and articulation of arguments during the class debate, as well as their ability to respond to questions and defend their stance.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist & Peer Rubric):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation, particularly /t/ in `trade` and /g/ in `global`, and stress on Wh-question words and modal verbs.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective use of target vocabulary to support arguments.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of passive voice, modals of necessity, and relative clauses.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence of arguments.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to engage respectfully in conversation and acknowledge different opinions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaborative interaction within the team.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete an exit ticket with the following prompts:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new idea I learned about Panama's global importance today was..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I successfully used (passive voice / modal verb / relative clause) when I said..."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of the debate was most challenging for you, and why?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can you improve your ability to present arguments about Panama's global role in English?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The debate activity fostered active engagement and encouraged the use of complex grammatical structures and a wide range of vocabulary. Students generally demonstrated good control of passive voice, but some struggled with spontaneous generation of relative clauses during the debate. Pronunciation of stressed modal verbs needs more explicit practice. Grouping was effective, and peer feedback was constructive. For the next lesson, scaffolding for complex sentence construction will be necessary, perhaps through guided writing prompts to prepare for the writing focus.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson's debate has helped students articulate their ideas about Panama's importance. In Lesson 4, they will transition these spoken arguments into written form, focusing on constructing well-structured paragraphs to summarize and persuade, building on the vocabulary and grammar practiced today.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>